  "result": "Fixed. Short option names now come before long ones in `--help`, so you get `-v, --verbose` instead of `--verbose, -v`.\n\n- **Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py` sorted option names by prefix length with `reverse=True`, which put `--long` names ahead of `-s` names. I removed `reverse=True`.\n- **Test:** I added `test_join_options_short_before_long` to `tests/test_formatting.py`.\n- **Result:** The full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nI took \"weird order\" to mean the order of the names within each option. If you meant the order of the options themselves (which option appears first in the list), tell me and I'll look at that instead.",
